the := default-type path does NOT fit-check a literal exceeding the target int: x := 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF (2^64-1, valid union-range literal but not in int64) silently WRAPS to int -1 (compiles rc=0, no diagnostic) instead of being rejected, while the explicit-type path var x int = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF correctly rejects with "cannot assign untyped int to int". Silent integer-wrap miscompile. spec const.default.int-width (§6.2); claude-todo MAJOR.
